 When there are no expenses (an empty file, or nothing left after `--month`), the output is the single line `No expenses found.` and the exit status is 0.
 
+## JSON output
+
+`--format json` prints the same summary as one JSON document instead of the table:
+
+```
+{
+  "categories": [
+    {
+      "category": "Rent",
+      "count": 1,
+      "total": 1200.0
+    },
+    {
+      "category": "Groceries",
+      "count": 3,
+      "total": 168.7
+    }
+  ],
+  "count": 4,
+  "total": 1368.7
+}
+```
+
+The categories are in the same order as the text table. Amounts are plain numbers rounded to cents: no thousands separator, refunds negative. With no expenses the document is `{"categories": [], "count": 0, "total": 0}`. Errors are reported the same way in both formats.
+
 ## Options
 
 - `--month YYYY-MM` keeps only expenses dated in that month.
 - `--sort {total,name}` chooses the order described above (default `total`).
+- `--format {text,json}` chooses the output format (default `text`).
 
 ## Errors
 
